Package: IRTistic
Type: Package
Title: Item Response Theory and Many-Facet Rasch Measurement with Artful Graphics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Valerie", "Ofori Aboah", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ofori96valerie@gmail.com")
Description: A single toolkit for item response theory (IRT) and Rasch
    measurement. Estimates unidimensional and confirmatory multidimensional
    Rasch, 2PL, 3PL, graded response, partial credit, generalized partial
    credit and rating scale models by marginal maximum likelihood with an
    EM algorithm, and many-facet Rasch models (in the style of FACETS) for
    rater-mediated assessments. Provides person scoring (EAP, MAP, ML, WLE),
    infit/outfit statistics, separation and reliability, local dependence
    and residual dimensionality checks, differential item functioning,
    rater bias/interaction analysis, data simulation, and a consistent set
    of 'ggplot2' graphics including Wright maps, FACETS-style vertical
    rulers, item and category curves, information functions and fit bubble
    charts.
